//
// Sail 0.16 configuration of the reference model for the T3 core (3-csr-trap):
// RV32IM_Zicsr_Zicntr_Zihpm_Zifencei, machine mode only. ACT4 reads it as
// <dut_include_dir>/sail.json, and `make ref` runs the final ELFs with it.
// Derived from rv32emu v1.3's ACT4 target
// (tests/arch-test-target/rv32emu-rv32imafc/sail.json), which is for the same
// Sail release. mycpu-t3.yaml states the same choices for the test generator:
// change the two files together.
//
// What differs from that file, and why (tests/act4/README.md has the details):
//   base.hpmevent_width_bits 4         mhpmevent3..10 are plain 4-bit fields
//   base.writable_hpm_counters 0x7F8   mhpmcounter3..10 exist, 11..31 read 0
//   base.mcountinhibit                 implemented, writable bits 0x7FD
//   base.*counteren, medeleg, mideleg  0: there is no S or U mode
//   base.xtval_nonzero                 only the eight causes this hart can raise
//   base.mstatus                       FS and VS are hardwired Off (no F, no V)
//   memory.misaligned.exceptions       a misaligned load or store traps, and
//                                      outranks an access fault
//   memory.dtb_address 0x803F_F000     the last page of RAM: Sail writes no
//                                      device tree there unless asked to
//                                      (checked: the word reads 0), and
//                                      nothing is mapped at 0x1000
//   memory.regions                     CLINT (64 KiB at 0x0200_0000), UART and
//                                      SimCtrl (8 KiB at 0x1000_0000, plain I/O
//                                      memory to Sail), RAM (4 MiB at
//                                      0x8000_0000, as in link.ld)
//   platform.vendorid/archid/impid     0, as the CSRs read
//   platform.interrupts.machine        software, timer and external exist
//   platform.clint                     base 0x0200_0000 (33554432), 64 KiB
//   platform.simple_interrupt_generator
//                                      base 0x1000_1FE0 (268443616), an unused
//                                      SimCtrl offset: see rvmodel_macros.h
//   platform.instructions_per_tick 1   mtime advances once per instruction, as
//                                      it does per cycle on a core with CPI 1
//   platform.event_selectors []        Sail counts none of this core's events
//   extensions                         M, Zmmul, Zicsr, Zicntr, Zihpm, Zifencei
//                                      supported; everything else off; no
//                                      misa bit is writable
